WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.357 --> 00:00:04.659
- If you havin' a bad time
right now, it cannot last!

00:00:04.659 --> 00:00:06.650
Poor people talk about money all the time,

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.751
rich people talk about things.

00:00:08.751 --> 00:00:11.049
Wealthy people, they talk about ideas.

00:00:11.049 --> 00:00:13.284
Instead of waiting for
someone to give you a job,

00:00:13.284 --> 00:00:15.203
create your own work.

00:00:15.203 --> 00:00:17.410
- He was a Bohemian evangelical Christian

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.929
and ordained minister,

00:00:18.929 --> 00:00:21.914
he founded the Bahamas Faith
Ministries International.

00:00:21.914 --> 00:00:23.751
He was the CEO and chairman of the

00:00:23.751 --> 00:00:26.609
International Third World
Leaders Association,

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:28.446
he's Myles Munroe, and here's my take

00:00:28.446 --> 00:00:30.493
on his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:30.493 --> 00:00:31.987
Rule number five is my personal favorite,

00:00:31.987 --> 00:00:33.809
and make sure to stick around
all the way till the end

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:35.584
for some special bonus clips.

00:00:35.584 --> 00:00:36.940
And as always, as Myles is talking,

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.253
if he says something that really
really resonates with you,

00:00:39.253 --> 00:00:40.993
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:40.993 --> 00:00:42.094
and put quotes around it

00:00:42.094 --> 00:00:44.787
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:44.787 --> 00:00:45.620
Enjoy!

00:00:48.926 --> 00:00:51.676
(dramatic music)

00:00:58.656 --> 00:01:00.746
- Change is inevitable.

00:01:00.746 --> 00:01:04.380
Change is also the principle of life,

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:08.011
that means that everything
that is alive will change.

00:01:08.011 --> 00:01:11.928
And even things that are
not alive will change.

00:01:14.233 --> 00:01:17.264
You know, a lady came to me,

00:01:17.264 --> 00:01:19.611
she says, I came to the
Bahamas for the last 10 years,

00:01:19.611 --> 00:01:21.739
and I missed four years,

00:01:21.739 --> 00:01:26.008
and I came here this past month
and everything is different.

00:01:26.008 --> 00:01:28.910
The airport is new she said.

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:31.861
What happened to the old airport she says.

00:01:31.861 --> 00:01:35.776
In other words, even the
things not alive are changing.

00:01:35.776 --> 00:01:37.763
The way the river runs down the mountain

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:39.145
is wearing away the mountain.

00:01:39.145 --> 00:01:41.331
You go back to that
mountain 10 years later,

00:01:41.331 --> 00:01:43.248
and the river is wider.

00:01:44.402 --> 00:01:47.819
Change is in creation, it's part of life.

00:01:49.202 --> 00:01:51.255
So here is the question then,

00:01:51.255 --> 00:01:53.173
Ecclesiastes chapter three,

00:01:53.173 --> 00:01:56.901
it says to everything there is a season,

00:01:56.901 --> 00:02:01.068
and to every purpose, under
heaven, there is a time for it.

00:02:02.439 --> 00:02:05.022
To everything there's a season.

00:02:06.312 --> 00:02:07.941
How many things have a season?

00:02:07.941 --> 00:02:08.858
Everything!

00:02:09.698 --> 00:02:13.865
This is one of the best
news I ever got in my life.

00:02:14.803 --> 00:02:16.758
When I understood this, I was a teenager,

00:02:16.758 --> 00:02:17.950
and it changed my life,

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:21.126
but I understood that
everything is a season.

00:02:21.126 --> 00:02:21.959
Let me tell you why,

00:02:21.959 --> 00:02:26.126
if you havin' a bad time
right now, it cannot last!

00:02:27.802 --> 00:02:30.967
(audience applause)

00:02:30.967 --> 00:02:35.134
If you cannot find a job right
now, that is only a season.

00:02:38.117 --> 00:02:41.058
If your business is going
in the wrong direction,

00:02:41.058 --> 00:02:42.975
it's a season of slide.

00:02:46.375 --> 00:02:50.673
If nobody wants to marry
you, that's only a season.

00:02:50.673 --> 00:02:53.793
(audience laughing)

00:02:53.793 --> 00:02:56.502
They're going to come a season,
everybody want to marry you!

00:02:56.502 --> 00:03:00.169
You got choices (laughing).

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.353
If you have no money right now,

00:03:03.353 --> 00:03:06.999
the good news is I am seasonally broke!

00:03:06.999 --> 00:03:09.815
Tell your neighbor, it's only for a time.

00:03:09.815 --> 00:03:11.565
That's the good news!

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.539
That's why we are always reminded,

00:03:15.539 --> 00:03:18.206
never make a permanent decision,

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.254
in a temporary problem.

00:03:22.254 --> 00:03:25.421
Success is a not something you pursue.

00:03:26.277 --> 00:03:30.194
Success is a matter
becoming a person of value.

00:03:32.368 --> 00:03:33.780
We should not be pursing money,

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.415
we should pursue purpose,
we should pursue vision.

00:03:37.415 --> 00:03:40.314
For ourselves, and for our
countries, for our communities.

00:03:40.314 --> 00:03:44.910
We should be pursuing things,
we need to pursue ideas.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:45.743
- That's right.

00:03:45.743 --> 00:03:48.066
- I always say there are three
types of people in the world,

00:03:48.066 --> 00:03:50.014
there's poor people, there's rich people,

00:03:50.014 --> 00:03:51.806
and there's wealthy people.

00:03:51.806 --> 00:03:53.657
Poor people talk about money all the time.

00:03:53.657 --> 00:03:55.756
Rich people talk about things.

00:03:55.756 --> 00:03:58.721
Wealthy people, they talk about ideas.

00:03:58.721 --> 00:04:00.205
Rich people, poor people,

00:04:00.205 --> 00:04:01.982
and wealthy people think differently.

00:04:01.982 --> 00:04:04.825
For example, poor people,
they pursue money.

00:04:04.825 --> 00:04:06.252
Rich people pursue things.

00:04:06.252 --> 00:04:08.817
Wealthy people pursue ideas.

00:04:08.817 --> 00:04:11.364
And so constantly there's a
different way of thinking.

00:04:11.364 --> 00:04:13.856
I hope that the third world countries,

00:04:13.856 --> 00:04:15.611
and the young people of our nations,

00:04:15.611 --> 00:04:17.510
they become ideas people.

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:20.523
You know, ideas control
the world, not money.

00:04:20.523 --> 00:04:21.356
- That's right.

00:04:21.356 --> 00:04:23.606
- And ideas attract money.

00:04:23.606 --> 00:04:27.539
So I think if we minimize
this desire to get money,

00:04:27.539 --> 00:04:30.881
and elevate the creativity of new ideas,

00:04:30.881 --> 00:04:35.048
we'll find that financial results
will naturally flow to it.

00:04:36.017 --> 00:04:39.711
Bill Gates didn't pursue
money, he pursued an idea.

00:04:39.711 --> 00:04:41.831
Steven Jobs, the late Steven Jobs,

00:04:41.831 --> 00:04:44.663
who invented the Apple
computer, and the iPhone,

00:04:44.663 --> 00:04:45.923
he never went after money,

00:04:45.923 --> 00:04:47.653
he developed an idea.

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:51.033
And if you think of all the
wealthy people in the world,

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:54.457
it was ideas that made
them wealthy, not money.

00:04:54.457 --> 00:04:57.407
So I think we need to reverse it,

00:04:57.407 --> 00:05:00.488
don't pursue money and
then try to get an idea.

00:05:00.488 --> 00:05:02.924
Get an idea and money
will pursue the idea.

00:05:02.924 --> 00:05:06.649
And you become a by-product,
as far as wealth.

00:05:06.649 --> 00:05:08.982
I tell all the young people,

00:05:10.065 --> 00:05:12.184
I say to you right now,
stop looking for employment.

00:05:12.184 --> 00:05:14.792
Why don't you position
yourself differently,

00:05:14.792 --> 00:05:16.792
and look for deployment.

00:05:18.165 --> 00:05:20.605
To be employed means that somebody else

00:05:20.605 --> 00:05:22.920
is benefiting from your energy.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:27.817
To deploy yourself, means that
you are using your own energy

00:05:27.817 --> 00:05:29.333
to be productive.

00:05:29.333 --> 00:05:32.127
So instead of waiting for
someone to give you a job,

00:05:32.127 --> 00:05:34.041
create your own work.

00:05:34.041 --> 00:05:36.009
That's why people, it's different between

00:05:36.009 --> 00:05:37.743
your work and your job.

00:05:37.743 --> 00:05:41.435
Your job is what they train you to do.

00:05:41.435 --> 00:05:44.481
Your work is what you were born to do.

00:05:44.481 --> 00:05:46.536
Your job is your skill,

00:05:46.536 --> 00:05:48.395
which they can fire you from at any time.

00:05:48.395 --> 00:05:51.934
But your work is your gift,
no one can take that from you.

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:56.290
Your job is where you get
compensation for activity.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.745
Your work is when you get fulfillment

00:05:58.745 --> 00:06:00.460
cuz you love it so much.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.742
Your job, you can retire from.

00:06:02.742 --> 00:06:04.349
Your work, you can never
retire from your work,

00:06:04.349 --> 00:06:06.081
cuz your work is you.

00:06:06.081 --> 00:06:08.802
So when a person discovers their work,

00:06:08.802 --> 00:06:10.529
they no longer need a job.

00:06:10.529 --> 00:06:12.429
Cuz their work makes them productive.

00:06:12.429 --> 00:06:14.161
So there are young people in this country

00:06:14.161 --> 00:06:16.343
who are full of talents, full of gifts,

00:06:16.343 --> 00:06:19.170
and I want to say this too,

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:22.170
every problem in life is a business.

00:06:23.766 --> 00:06:27.297
All businesses are simply
someone solving a problem.

00:06:27.297 --> 00:06:29.945
So the more problems that are in Kenya,

00:06:29.945 --> 00:06:33.327
the more businesses available
for young people to begin.

00:06:33.327 --> 00:06:35.451
And this is what I think we are lacking.

00:06:35.451 --> 00:06:38.154
We are trained to get a job,

00:06:38.154 --> 00:06:41.108
we're not trained to start a business.

00:06:41.108 --> 00:06:44.168
We are trained to let
other people employ us,

00:06:44.168 --> 00:06:46.906
not trained to deploy ourselves.

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:51.669
Do we sit down and let
change just happen to us?

00:06:51.669 --> 00:06:55.836
Or are we just watching
change happening around us?

00:06:57.201 --> 00:07:02.070
Or are we aware that change
is happening within us?

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:04.831
Or are we going to be
those pro-active people,

00:07:04.831 --> 00:07:08.961
who make sure that we
affect what happens to us?

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:12.964
Change also produces four types of people.

00:07:12.964 --> 00:07:13.923
They are in this room,

00:07:13.923 --> 00:07:18.090
first of all, there are people
who who watch things happen.

00:07:21.931 --> 00:07:23.480
Now let me say something about change,

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.533
this is important here.

00:07:25.533 --> 00:07:28.033
Not all change is improvement.

00:07:30.386 --> 00:07:32.219
You used to weigh 128.

00:07:36.845 --> 00:07:38.512
And now you changed.

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.264
And for some of you,
that's not an improvement.

00:07:41.264 --> 00:07:44.938
You lost your wardrobe (laughing)

00:07:44.938 --> 00:07:48.535
you lost your ability
to climb up steps fast.

00:07:48.535 --> 00:07:53.002
Even lost the quality
of health that you had.

00:07:53.002 --> 00:07:56.752
Change doesn't mean
improvement all the time.

00:07:58.363 --> 00:08:01.160
But the problem is, without change,

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.493
there can be no improvement.

00:08:05.745 --> 00:08:09.495
So you have to decide
what to do with change.

00:08:11.203 --> 00:08:12.786
Change will happen,

00:08:13.944 --> 00:08:18.111
and if you are not careful,
it could be destructive.

00:08:20.602 --> 00:08:21.631
So you have to determine

00:08:21.631 --> 00:08:25.336
what kind of change do I want in my life?

00:08:25.336 --> 00:08:27.032
And I want you as a young person,

00:08:27.032 --> 00:08:29.366
as a mother and a father,
as a business person,

00:08:29.366 --> 00:08:31.186
to think about your company even,

00:08:31.186 --> 00:08:33.812
or your family, or your
educational pursuit.

00:08:33.812 --> 00:08:36.473
And what kind of classes
do you want to take

00:08:36.473 --> 00:08:37.440
in college this year?

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:39.218
What kind of grades do you want?

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:42.070
What kind of relationship you
want to have in your life?

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:44.603
Who do you want to drop and
who do you want to pick up

00:08:44.603 --> 00:08:45.436
in your relationships?

00:08:45.436 --> 00:08:47.204
What kind of people do you
want to associate with?

00:08:47.204 --> 00:08:48.579
Where do you want to travel,

00:08:48.579 --> 00:08:49.551
that you've never been?

00:08:49.551 --> 00:08:51.872
What are the books you need
to read you never read before?

00:08:51.872 --> 00:08:54.455
That changes come with choices.

00:08:57.943 --> 00:09:00.677
So what kind person are you?

00:09:00.677 --> 00:09:03.051
We shouldn't try to get everything now.

00:09:03.051 --> 00:09:04.520
You know, I got into college,

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.892
I spent eight years in universities,

00:09:06.892 --> 00:09:09.072
I have three bachelors
degrees, a masters degree,

00:09:09.072 --> 00:09:11.917
five doctorate degrees, bestowed upon me,

00:09:11.917 --> 00:09:14.899
by many different universities.

00:09:14.899 --> 00:09:17.250
And many of my friends
are in the school with me,

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:19.281
high school, they went straight to jobs.

00:09:19.281 --> 00:09:20.863
I went to college.

00:09:20.863 --> 00:09:22.826
You know, they started makin' money early.

00:09:22.826 --> 00:09:25.467
I delayed my money makin' for five years.

00:09:25.467 --> 00:09:27.375
And now what they make in a year,

00:09:27.375 --> 00:09:29.130
I probably make in an hour.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:32.327
And so you know, we
need to be more focused

00:09:32.327 --> 00:09:33.940
on developing ourselves,

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:37.616
rather than trying to grab money now.

00:09:37.616 --> 00:09:41.638
Focus on self improvement, self expansion,

00:09:41.638 --> 00:09:44.233
rather than trying to
get your pocket fix back.

00:09:44.233 --> 00:09:47.900
Because the more valuable
you make yourself,

00:09:49.498 --> 00:09:52.002
the more value you attract.

00:09:52.002 --> 00:09:54.398
You are not paid for how hard you worked,

00:09:54.398 --> 00:09:57.660
you are paid for what you are
worth to the organization.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:00.736
And the more intellectual
development you have

00:10:00.736 --> 00:10:02.720
the more spiritual development you have,

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.676
the more psychological development,

00:10:04.676 --> 00:10:05.950
your emotional stability,

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:08.054
you become more valuable to the world.

00:10:08.054 --> 00:10:09.945
And let me say this finally,

00:10:09.945 --> 00:10:12.945
if you become valuable to the world,

00:10:13.786 --> 00:10:16.279
the world will pay you to be yourself.

00:10:16.279 --> 00:10:20.728
So it's important for you
to become a person of value

00:10:20.728 --> 00:10:22.866
not to seek value in things.

00:10:22.866 --> 00:10:26.264
I get paid for what I
know, not for what I do.

00:10:26.264 --> 00:10:28.438
And I think this is
what we need to perceive

00:10:28.438 --> 00:10:30.243
as being most valuable.

00:10:30.243 --> 00:10:34.057
Do you know what they
actually call intellect?

00:10:34.057 --> 00:10:35.473
They call it capital.

00:10:35.473 --> 00:10:39.053
You know intellectual capital
is really a commodity.

00:10:39.053 --> 00:10:42.133
And so I want to
encourage our young people

00:10:42.133 --> 00:10:46.997
to focus on discovering
the purpose for your life.

00:10:46.997 --> 00:10:48.555
Why God created you,

00:10:48.555 --> 00:10:51.604
and then discover your
gifts, and then refine them,

00:10:51.604 --> 00:10:53.771
develop them, practice them,

00:10:53.771 --> 00:10:56.790
and then even begin to sow
them free into your community.

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:59.618
Develop yourself and in a short time,

00:10:59.618 --> 00:11:03.616
you will discover that
people will pursue you,

00:11:03.616 --> 00:11:05.410
because when you develop your fruit,

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:08.633
and you maximize your
fruit or your gift in life

00:11:08.633 --> 00:11:10.036
just like a tree.

00:11:10.036 --> 00:11:12.419
Trees never bring their fruit to you.

00:11:12.419 --> 00:11:13.252
- That's right.

00:11:13.252 --> 00:11:14.584
- They just simply manifest it.

00:11:14.584 --> 00:11:17.038
You are attracted to the tree.

00:11:17.038 --> 00:11:19.452
So when you develop your
gifts and refine your gifts,

00:11:19.452 --> 00:11:22.676
you don't need to look for
followers, they'll find you.

00:11:22.676 --> 00:11:25.656
After all, leadership is
not about finding followers,

00:11:25.656 --> 00:11:28.119
it's about followers being
attracted to what you have.

00:11:28.119 --> 00:11:30.370
And this is true commodity.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:34.263
Power for me to be successful
was not in the teachers,

00:11:34.263 --> 00:11:36.277
it was not in the educational system,

00:11:36.277 --> 00:11:39.075
it was not in my culture,
it was not in my society,

00:11:39.075 --> 00:11:40.920
it was within me, and I began to think,

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:44.391
God if you are a good God, why am I poor?

00:11:44.391 --> 00:11:48.734
If you are a great God, why are
these people better than me?

00:11:48.734 --> 00:11:52.874
If you make me in your
image, why are they special?

00:11:52.874 --> 00:11:54.546
And I'm a monkey?

00:11:54.546 --> 00:11:58.227
And that night, no thunder, no lightening,

00:11:58.227 --> 00:12:00.613
no earthquakes, nothing.

00:12:00.613 --> 00:12:02.863
I just heard a voice in my mind.

00:12:02.863 --> 00:12:06.696
And the voice said, I
asked you to believe me.

00:12:08.132 --> 00:12:10.632
And you'll be saved, not them.

00:12:13.008 --> 00:12:14.952
And that night, I made a commitment

00:12:14.952 --> 00:12:16.733
to believe what God said.

00:12:16.733 --> 00:12:19.990
13 years old, I said,
okay I believe that I

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:23.306
have the power to experience far beyond

00:12:23.306 --> 00:12:25.856
all I can ever ask, think or imagine.

00:12:25.856 --> 00:12:30.023
13 years old, and that's
when my pursuit of God began.

00:12:30.941 --> 00:12:32.438
- When was it that you realized

00:12:32.438 --> 00:12:35.461
you wanted to become a preacher?

00:12:35.461 --> 00:12:38.146
- You know, I didn't want
to become a preacher.

00:12:38.146 --> 00:12:39.366
Matter of fact, today I still don't

00:12:39.366 --> 00:12:40.656
consider myself a preacher.

00:12:40.656 --> 00:12:44.216
I think it drove me to have a passion

00:12:44.216 --> 00:12:48.128
to help everybody whose been oppressed.

00:12:48.128 --> 00:12:51.295
My passion is to make sure that no one

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:56.404
should live under what I experienced.

00:12:56.404 --> 00:12:59.427
I never desired to be a minister.

00:12:59.427 --> 00:13:01.962
I desired to help people.

00:13:01.962 --> 00:13:03.540
You should never judge your success

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.873
by other people's accolades.

00:13:07.128 --> 00:13:09.872
You judge your success by
God's instruction to your life

00:13:09.872 --> 00:13:13.403
and how well along you
are with that instruction.

00:13:13.403 --> 00:13:15.331
Because I found there's something in life

00:13:15.331 --> 00:13:18.815
the average human being is so mediocre

00:13:18.815 --> 00:13:22.482
that to be a genius,
just do a little extra.

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:26.827
Yall missed that.

00:13:26.827 --> 00:13:28.577
People are so normal,

00:13:30.018 --> 00:13:34.365
to be an expert, just
go one inch abnormal.

00:13:34.365 --> 00:13:36.698
And they think you're great.

00:13:38.468 --> 00:13:42.051
So don't judge your success by the masses,

00:13:42.051 --> 00:13:44.368
what they think of you.

00:13:44.368 --> 00:13:47.724
Judge yourself by what God told you to do.

00:13:47.724 --> 00:13:48.992
Can I put it another way?

00:13:48.992 --> 00:13:52.040
When experience is your best teacher,

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.373
then progress is imprisoned.

00:13:57.391 --> 00:13:59.724
Experience could be a curse.

00:14:00.927 --> 00:14:03.974
I've been taught by my parents years ago

00:14:03.974 --> 00:14:06.731
that experience is the best teacher.

00:14:06.731 --> 00:14:09.474
I don't believe that anymore.

00:14:09.474 --> 00:14:13.287
Experience could cause
you to stop progressing,

00:14:13.287 --> 00:14:16.614
because you keep judging your
dreams by your experience.

00:14:16.614 --> 00:14:19.106
Or your vision by your experience.

00:14:19.106 --> 00:14:22.689
And you end up saying,
I tried that before.

00:14:23.665 --> 00:14:26.748
Or I never saw anyone do it that way.

00:14:27.684 --> 00:14:29.213
And you begin to use your experience

00:14:29.213 --> 00:14:31.046
to stop your progress.

00:14:31.885 --> 00:14:36.052
This is why God always makes
history with young people.

00:14:37.556 --> 00:14:41.757
Because old people got
too much experience.

00:14:41.757 --> 00:14:44.505
Yall remember the story
with David and Goliath?

00:14:44.505 --> 00:14:46.310
The problem with Saul, who was the king,

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:48.268
was that he had experience.

00:14:48.268 --> 00:14:51.743
And he tried to put his
experience on David.

00:14:51.743 --> 00:14:54.656
He told David, wear my
armor, wear my shield,

00:14:54.656 --> 00:14:56.366
use my sword, David put it on,

00:14:56.366 --> 00:14:58.547
David said this thing is too heavy.

00:14:58.547 --> 00:15:00.577
And he went out and fought the giant,

00:15:00.577 --> 00:15:04.077
with something the giant never saw before.

00:15:05.377 --> 00:15:06.785
A sling!

00:15:06.785 --> 00:15:09.853
How do you fight a rock with a sword?

00:15:09.853 --> 00:15:12.103
(laughing)

00:15:13.238 --> 00:15:16.496
The giant says, "What is
this thing he's using?"

00:15:16.496 --> 00:15:19.393
The giant is trained
experience with a sword,

00:15:19.393 --> 00:15:21.791
so he expected an experienced swordsman

00:15:21.791 --> 00:15:23.632
to come and fight him.

00:15:23.632 --> 00:15:25.737
But here comes a little boy,

00:15:25.737 --> 00:15:28.329
with equipment he ain't never seen before.

00:15:28.329 --> 00:15:31.515
We need some people like
that in the 21st century.

00:15:31.515 --> 00:15:32.364
(audience applause)

00:15:32.364 --> 00:15:33.932
who come with some things
that they ain't never seen

00:15:33.932 --> 00:15:35.909
at the office.

00:15:35.909 --> 00:15:39.491
Think of some ideas that'll
wreck the whole system.

00:15:39.491 --> 00:15:42.236
That's why Steven Jobs
will always be in history

00:15:42.236 --> 00:15:43.462
as a great inventor.

00:15:43.462 --> 00:15:46.379
He keep defying his own experience.

00:15:50.614 --> 00:15:52.114
I was reading his,

00:15:53.666 --> 00:15:57.005
watching a documentary
on him two weeks ago,

00:15:57.005 --> 00:15:58.936
and they said that when
the iPhone came out,

00:15:58.936 --> 00:16:00.961
they said to him that's it,

00:16:00.961 --> 00:16:03.520
you the ultimate, this is it.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:07.757
He said no, and he came up
with this idea about the iPad.

00:16:07.757 --> 00:16:10.850
And he said the people
in the company said,

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:12.433
it will never work!

00:16:13.743 --> 00:16:14.611
Why?

00:16:14.611 --> 00:16:16.444
It's an abnormal size.

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:20.549
Either you got a computer or an iPhone,

00:16:20.549 --> 00:16:22.018
put it in your pocket or
put it in your briefcase.

00:16:22.018 --> 00:16:23.817
See this thing in the
middle, ain't going to work.

00:16:23.817 --> 00:16:26.567
He says look, we going to make this.

00:16:27.628 --> 00:16:31.795
Now the iPad is the most
common machinery people use

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:36.473
in the world!

00:16:38.597 --> 00:16:42.764
Sometime you got to defy your
own board, to take progress.

00:16:46.596 --> 00:16:49.596
Experience, consult your experience,

00:16:50.809 --> 00:16:52.872
but never let it rule you.

00:16:52.872 --> 00:16:57.421
Chesma says, sweet are
the uses of adversity.

00:16:57.421 --> 00:16:58.754
Ooh I like that.

00:17:00.636 --> 00:17:03.303
Sweet are the uses of adversity,

00:17:04.271 --> 00:17:07.425
he says, you must learn to use adversity

00:17:07.425 --> 00:17:09.283
for your benefit.

00:17:09.283 --> 00:17:11.572
One of the wealthiest
men in the United States,

00:17:11.572 --> 00:17:14.232
I just finished reading his book, again,

00:17:14.232 --> 00:17:15.565
his new edition,

00:17:17.026 --> 00:17:19.776
it's called "Cheaters Never Win."

00:17:21.579 --> 00:17:23.118
He's a multi-billionaire,

00:17:23.118 --> 00:17:26.895
he probably has products
in this room today.

00:17:26.895 --> 00:17:29.864
Or in this building somewhere.

00:17:29.864 --> 00:17:34.031
He is the largest manufacturer
of plastic, paper, cups,

00:17:35.596 --> 00:17:38.929
and paper plates and forks in the world.

00:17:41.129 --> 00:17:45.213
The company is called
The Huntsman Enterprise.

00:17:45.213 --> 00:17:48.790
Multi-billionaire, here's
what he says in his book,

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:49.902
I just finished reading,

00:17:49.902 --> 00:17:53.595
he says if there is a
silver lining to bad times,

00:17:53.595 --> 00:17:57.917
it is this, when facing severe challenges,

00:17:57.917 --> 00:18:01.167
your mind is normally at it's sharpest.

00:18:02.569 --> 00:18:05.236
I wonder why he's a billionaire?

00:18:06.902 --> 00:18:11.069
When facing challenges, he
says your mind kicks in,

00:18:13.685 --> 00:18:16.271
and thinks beyond the norm.

00:18:16.271 --> 00:18:18.658
He also says, another statement
I thought was interesting,

00:18:18.658 --> 00:18:22.730
he said humans seldom have
created anything of lasting

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:26.063
value unless they were tried or hurting.

00:18:30.512 --> 00:18:32.262
Benefits from crisis,

00:18:33.327 --> 00:18:37.622
this is when you are supposed
to become a greater leader,

00:18:37.622 --> 00:18:41.789
a better leader, because
your skills must be tested.

00:18:44.733 --> 00:18:49.552
I put it another way, Abraham
Lincoln was an amazing guy.

00:18:49.552 --> 00:18:54.522
He became the greatest president,
in the midst of trials.

00:18:54.522 --> 00:18:57.339
Today, I still am convinced,
he is the greatest

00:18:57.339 --> 00:19:00.042
President of the United States in history.

00:19:00.042 --> 00:19:04.125
Because he used adversity
to create a federation,

00:19:05.480 --> 00:19:09.313
that lasted 300 years
and still we're working,

00:19:11.147 --> 00:19:14.035
but it came out of the fires of crisis.

00:19:14.035 --> 00:19:16.126
My definition of
leadership is very simple,

00:19:16.126 --> 00:19:17.338
yet complicated.

00:19:17.338 --> 00:19:18.318
I believe that leadership

00:19:18.318 --> 00:19:20.731
is the capacity to influence others

00:19:20.731 --> 00:19:22.999
through inspiration, not manipulation.

00:19:22.999 --> 00:19:25.579
And that inspiration comes from a passion

00:19:25.579 --> 00:19:27.633
which is motivation by a sense of vision,

00:19:27.633 --> 00:19:29.117
and a sense of purpose.

00:19:29.117 --> 00:19:31.872
So leadership is first
personal, then it's corporate.

00:19:31.872 --> 00:19:33.761
Leadership is not something you pursue,

00:19:33.761 --> 00:19:35.006
it's something you discover.

00:19:35.006 --> 00:19:37.733
Leaders are born when a
human discovers something

00:19:37.733 --> 00:19:41.074
more important than
their personal ambition.

00:19:41.074 --> 00:19:42.258
- You don't pursue it?

00:19:42.258 --> 00:19:45.076
- No true leaders do not seek followers.

00:19:45.076 --> 00:19:48.057
Leaders are actually
pursuing a passion toward

00:19:48.057 --> 00:19:50.002
a purpose that gives
them a sense of destiny.

00:19:50.002 --> 00:19:52.558
For example, one of the
greatest leaders of example

00:19:52.558 --> 00:19:53.963
that I use is Nelson Mandela,

00:19:53.963 --> 00:19:55.431
one of your great presidents.

00:19:55.431 --> 00:19:57.931
He never sought followers, think about it.

00:19:57.931 --> 00:20:00.491
He discovered a purpose
that was more important

00:20:00.491 --> 00:20:03.657
than his private preservation
and private ambition.

00:20:03.657 --> 00:20:06.320
He pursued that purpose privately.

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:07.654
It attracted people.

00:20:07.654 --> 00:20:09.612
So leaders don't seek followers,

00:20:09.612 --> 00:20:10.837
followers are attracted to leaders.

00:20:10.837 --> 00:20:14.116
Leaders are more concerned
about discovering a purpose

00:20:14.116 --> 00:20:16.037
to improve the life of humanity,

00:20:16.037 --> 00:20:18.132
that's more important than
their personal ambition.

00:20:18.132 --> 00:20:20.591
So they sacrifice themselves
to accomplish something

00:20:20.591 --> 00:20:21.660
for the greater good.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:23.675
We find that very rarely.

00:20:23.675 --> 00:20:25.982
Most people we call leaders are simply

00:20:25.982 --> 00:20:27.048
professional manipulators.

00:20:27.048 --> 00:20:28.436
And they actually are more concerned

00:20:28.436 --> 00:20:31.443
with their own promotion
than promoting the people.

00:20:31.443 --> 00:20:32.704
- As you look back over your life,

00:20:32.704 --> 00:20:34.891
if there's just one thing
that you could do differently,

00:20:34.891 --> 00:20:36.308
what would it be?

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:41.341
- Hmm, that's always a tough question,

00:20:41.341 --> 00:20:43.024
I get that question asked a lot.

00:20:43.024 --> 00:20:45.433
I'm not sure, you know,

00:20:45.433 --> 00:20:49.918
because everything that
happened in my life,

00:20:49.918 --> 00:20:53.066
produced me, even the negatives,

00:20:53.066 --> 00:20:55.192
even the things that I might've failed in.

00:20:55.192 --> 00:20:56.654
The things I made mistakes with,

00:20:56.654 --> 00:20:59.418
they were fantastic classrooms for me.

00:20:59.418 --> 00:21:01.507
And I believe the best thing in life to do

00:21:01.507 --> 00:21:04.514
is not to regret and try
to change what happened,

00:21:04.514 --> 00:21:06.384
but to interpret it properly,

00:21:06.384 --> 00:21:09.321
maximize it and use it
to serve other people.

00:21:09.321 --> 00:21:12.654
And that's what I want to do with my past.

00:21:14.698 --> 00:21:16.189
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:21:16.189 --> 00:21:19.194
I made this video because
Abel Solomon asked me to.

00:21:19.194 --> 00:21:20.420
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:22.134
that you want me to profile next,

00:21:22.134 --> 00:21:23.427
leave it down in the comments below,

00:21:23.427 --> 00:21:24.598
I'll see what I can do.

00:21:24.598 --> 00:21:26.459
I'd also love to know,
what did you hear today

00:21:26.459 --> 00:21:27.811
that inspired you the most?

00:21:27.811 --> 00:21:29.647
What was the biggest
lesson that you learned

00:21:29.647 --> 00:21:31.121
after watching this video?

00:21:31.121 --> 00:21:33.598
I'd love to hear from you,
please leave it in the comments.

00:21:33.598 --> 00:21:35.969
And I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:21:35.969 --> 00:21:37.711
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Max Jung,

00:21:37.711 --> 00:21:39.970
Max, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:42.121
it really really really means a lot to me.

00:21:42.121 --> 00:21:44.347
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:21:44.347 --> 00:21:47.388
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:21:47.388 --> 00:21:49.350
and whatever your one word is,

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:51.683
much love, I'll see ya soon.

00:21:58.075 --> 00:22:00.700
- I want to focus on discovering

00:22:00.700 --> 00:22:05.220
and releasing, how to release
your hidden greatness.

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:06.922
Every human being in this room,

00:22:06.922 --> 00:22:09.839
and those watching by the internet,

00:22:11.001 --> 00:22:12.692
you have inside of you,

00:22:12.692 --> 00:22:15.692
I have no doubt about it, greatness.

00:22:16.825 --> 00:22:21.463
But most people will die with
their greatness on the inside.

00:22:21.463 --> 00:22:24.952
And this is why we have this conference,

00:22:24.952 --> 00:22:26.958
because we don't want you
to be one of those persons

00:22:26.958 --> 00:22:29.812
who die with their greatness.

00:22:29.812 --> 00:22:33.105
Let me say a few comments about greatness.

00:22:33.105 --> 00:22:36.848
Every human desires two things in life,

00:22:36.848 --> 00:22:38.079
I want you to write 'em down.

00:22:38.079 --> 00:22:40.762
Two things, every human wants,

00:22:40.762 --> 00:22:44.210
six billion of us, and now seven billion

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:48.082
since last mid-April, on this planet,

00:22:48.082 --> 00:22:49.149
want two things.

00:22:49.149 --> 00:22:52.374
And everything you do is
motivated by these two things.

00:22:52.374 --> 00:22:54.547
One, we want power.

00:22:54.547 --> 00:22:57.729
Every young person, every
old person wants power.

00:22:57.729 --> 00:22:59.937
We got to talk about what power is.

00:22:59.937 --> 00:23:02.601
And the second thing we want is greatness.

00:23:02.601 --> 00:23:04.273
We don't talk about these too much,

00:23:04.273 --> 00:23:07.308
but every human being wants power,

00:23:07.308 --> 00:23:08.719
and they want greatness.

00:23:08.719 --> 00:23:12.919
This is why we are motivated
to wear certain clothing.

00:23:12.919 --> 00:23:15.200
We call 'em power clothing.

00:23:15.200 --> 00:23:18.627
This is why we try to join a gang,

00:23:18.627 --> 00:23:22.167
cuz being in a gang of
people gives you power

00:23:22.167 --> 00:23:24.177
to threaten other people.

00:23:24.177 --> 00:23:27.347
This is why we would
actually want to steal money

00:23:27.347 --> 00:23:31.517
or gain money, cuz money
gives you power to buy things

00:23:31.517 --> 00:23:34.939
that you want to make you feel important.

00:23:34.939 --> 00:23:38.122
Everything we do is motivated
by these two things.

00:23:38.122 --> 00:23:40.264
Power and greatness.

00:23:40.264 --> 00:23:42.571
Now I want to mention
something about power,

00:23:42.571 --> 00:23:43.693
what is power?

00:23:43.693 --> 00:23:46.937
Power, I want you to
quote it with me out loud,

00:23:46.937 --> 00:23:49.238
up on the board, so you can remember it,

00:23:49.238 --> 00:23:51.191
when you leave here, what is power?

00:23:51.191 --> 00:23:52.024
Read it!

00:23:52.024 --> 00:23:55.777
Power is the ability and the capacity

00:23:55.777 --> 00:23:59.518
to control circumstances
and the environment,

00:23:59.518 --> 00:24:00.897
that's power.

00:24:00.897 --> 00:24:02.316
Power is what?

00:24:02.316 --> 00:24:05.398
The ability to control circumstances

00:24:05.398 --> 00:24:07.785
and to control your environment.

00:24:07.785 --> 00:24:09.518
That's what power is,
and everybody wants it.

00:24:09.518 --> 00:24:12.475
The politician wants
it, the banker wants it.

00:24:12.475 --> 00:24:15.842
The parent wants it, the
young person wants it.

00:24:15.842 --> 00:24:18.210
Everybody wants power to
control circumstances.

00:24:18.210 --> 00:24:19.702
What is greatness?

00:24:19.702 --> 00:24:22.960
Write this down,
greatness, out loud please,

00:24:22.960 --> 00:24:27.438
is a sense of value,
importance and significance.

00:24:27.438 --> 00:24:28.855
That's greatness.

00:24:29.875 --> 00:24:31.460
Greatness is when you feel

00:24:31.460 --> 00:24:34.465
that you are important to the world.

00:24:34.465 --> 00:24:35.425
You feel great when you feel

00:24:35.425 --> 00:24:38.665
that you are valuable to society.

00:24:38.665 --> 00:24:41.772
Greatness is when you feel
that you are significant

00:24:41.772 --> 00:24:43.092
to your generation.

00:24:43.092 --> 00:24:47.259
In other words, the desire
for all of us to be great,

00:24:48.375 --> 00:24:51.875
and to control our environment is natural.

00:24:53.570 --> 00:24:55.748
You as a 16 year old,

00:24:55.748 --> 00:24:59.275
your desire to become
the head of the class

00:24:59.275 --> 00:25:01.050
is the desire for greatness.

00:25:01.050 --> 00:25:04.471
You as an 18 year old, your
desire to go to college

00:25:04.471 --> 00:25:06.936
and get a degree, so you
can get a better job,

00:25:06.936 --> 00:25:07.843
so you can make more money,

00:25:07.843 --> 00:25:09.306
so you can buy things you want,

00:25:09.306 --> 00:25:11.818
is a desire for control.

00:25:11.818 --> 00:25:13.820
A desire for greatness.

00:25:13.820 --> 00:25:15.899
And this is why people get in trouble.

00:25:15.899 --> 00:25:19.117
They're pursuing power and greatness.

00:25:19.117 --> 00:25:20.789
Now let me repeat again,

00:25:20.789 --> 00:25:24.622
the pursuit of power and
greatness is natural.

00:25:25.786 --> 00:25:28.065
As a matter of fact, if
you don't want to be great,

00:25:28.065 --> 00:25:30.526
something's wrong with you.

00:25:30.526 --> 00:25:33.609
If you have no desire to be powerful,

00:25:35.580 --> 00:25:37.657
something's wrong with you.

00:25:37.657 --> 00:25:40.906
Every person here desires these things.

00:25:40.906 --> 00:25:44.355
I put it this way, God is
not against your desire

00:25:44.355 --> 00:25:45.522
for greatness.

00:25:46.612 --> 00:25:50.656
He's not against your desire for power.

00:25:50.656 --> 00:25:53.323
Cuz God created you to be great.

00:25:55.000 --> 00:25:59.160
Potential is who you are
but no one knows it yet.

00:25:59.160 --> 00:26:02.071
Potential is who you could become

00:26:02.071 --> 00:26:03.466
but you haven't become it yet.

00:26:03.466 --> 00:26:04.956
Potential is how far you can go,

00:26:04.956 --> 00:26:05.960
but you haven't gone yet.

00:26:05.960 --> 00:26:09.042
In other words, potential
is never what you've done,

00:26:09.042 --> 00:26:11.050
cuz once you've done something,

00:26:11.050 --> 00:26:13.633
it ceases to be your potential.

00:26:14.613 --> 00:26:18.067
Potential therefore has to do
with what you haven't done yet

00:26:18.067 --> 00:26:19.667
that you can still yet do.

00:26:19.667 --> 00:26:21.823
That's why I am after you.

00:26:21.823 --> 00:26:25.186
I came after you because I'm
bored with what you've done

00:26:25.186 --> 00:26:26.686
I'm bored with it.

00:26:27.660 --> 00:26:28.955
You've got a Ph.D so what?

00:26:28.955 --> 00:26:29.863
It's over!

00:26:29.863 --> 00:26:30.863
What's left?

00:26:34.449 --> 00:26:36.719
Potential therefore is not
about what you've achieved,

00:26:36.719 --> 00:26:38.969
it's what you haven't achieved yet,

00:26:38.969 --> 00:26:40.101
that you could achieve.

00:26:40.101 --> 00:26:41.341
This is why I say this,

00:26:41.341 --> 00:26:43.801
that the end of your
potential, write it down,

00:26:43.801 --> 00:26:45.551
is your last success.

00:26:47.419 --> 00:26:50.397
The greatest enemy of your
potential is your success.

00:26:50.397 --> 00:26:52.527
Cuz when you become
successful at something,

00:26:52.527 --> 00:26:54.360
it tempts you to stop.

00:26:56.867 --> 00:27:01.034
This is why I am always nervous
about people's accolades

00:27:01.904 --> 00:27:03.071
concerning me.

00:27:05.309 --> 00:27:09.059
I don't trust too many
awards people give me.

00:27:11.364 --> 00:27:15.434
I have so many degrees bestowed upon me.

00:27:15.434 --> 00:27:17.184
